// Flat Rate Machine — Crawl Presence Registry dataset builder
// (Retrieval Machine Element 5, build batch B1 per Dossier 05 §7;
// executed as Retrieval Machine build batch E5-B1, 2026-10-31).
//   node scripts/build-crawl-presence.js [--out <file>]
//   node scripts/build-crawl-presence.js --check
// Run from the-flat-rate-machine/. No dependencies beyond Node itself.
//
// WHAT THIS IS
// datasets-crawl-presence.json: the standing registry of the
// Retrieval Machine's corpora element (design: Dossier 05 §5). For
// this element, time is the dataset: what the open crawl holds about
// this domain — per Common Crawl collection, per URL class, per
// content era — under what robots posture, and what has never been
// measured. Presence is era-tagged and method-honest: an errored
// index query is a first-class row, never a blank, and an absent
// capture is an explicit zero on a collection row, never a
// fabricated capture row:
//   collection          — every collection in Common Crawl's
//                         collinfo at seed time, with its query
//                         state (queried-clean / partial /
//                         unverifiable-index-error), the verbatim
//                         query method, attempts, and the crawl
//                         window observed for this domain.
//   crawl_presence      — one row per capture the index returned:
//                         url, timestamp, status, digest, and the
//                         URL class + content era COMPUTED by this
//                         generator from the URL form and the
//                         capture timestamp vs the 2026-10-28
//                         cutover — never hand-tagged (§5.3 gate).
//   presence_summary    — the generated view: per collection x
//                         URL class counts + 200-counts; per-era
//                         and per-class totals. The P5 dilution
//                         curve and the P2 sampling mix, as data.
//   robots_policy       — the owner's P3 decision record (Option 1,
//                         open training, decided 2026-10-31) + the
//                         per-agent table parsed from the live
//                         robots.txt + the drift gate: this
//                         generator FAILS if the served file's
//                         digest (carried by the signed signal
//                         observation) differs from the deployed
//                         source file it parses — the file cannot
//                         quietly stop matching the decision.
//   signal_observation  — the reconciliation's 22-field signed log
//                         shape: the served robots.txt as observed,
//                         digest-chained and Ed25519-signed with the
//                         estate key (kid
//                         theflatratemovers-2026-10-29-1); the
//                         RFC 3161 timestamp_token is an optional
//                         23rd field, unpopulated (no TSA adopted).
//   filter_inspection   — empty by design: rows exist only when a
//                         real WET record has been inspected
//                         (Dossier 05 P4, batch E5-B4).
//   corpus_release_check — state not-checked by design: rows are
//                         added only when a real downstream-release
//                         check runs (§5.1 honesty rule).
//   gap_record          — Dossier 05's gaps P1–P6, each with its
//                         designed solution and status.
//   mechanism_pins      — the verified mechanism facts the
//                         reconciliation pinned (TDMRep, aipref,
//                         CAWG training-mining, the shared
//                         __usage_ai-training token, per-purpose
//                         signal adherence), each with its source.
//
// SEED: the capture rows and the first signal observation are
// observations — frozen evidence, injected into this file between
// the SEED markers by the batch assembler
// (out/batch-crawl-presence-2026-10-31/work/assemble-generator.py)
// from the sweep output + the signed observation record. Future
// observations append by the same procedure (sweep -> sign ->
// assemble -> regenerate -> reseal); historical rows are immutable.
//
// DETERMINISM: the file's dateModified is the newest evidence date
// among its inputs (2026-10-31), never the wall clock, so --check
// is byte-stable across days.
